# Selected Skills Policy

Use imported or built-in skills only when relevant to the active LEXOS work packet.

LEXOS-specific rules control over generic imported skills.

Priority order:

1. `.cursor/rules/`
2. `docs/implementation/`
3. `docs/lexos-system-spec/`
4. `docs/ai-ops/imported-reference/` skills and agents
5. `docs/source-briefings/` legacy material

## Adopted Skill Policy

Use these skill categories when relevant:

- Schema and migrations: `database-design`, `supabase`, `supabase-postgres-best-practices`, Postgres best practices.
- Backend/API: `api-patterns`, `nodejs-best-practices`, `clean-code`.
- Frontend/UI: `nextjs-react-expert`, `frontend-design`, `tailwind-patterns`, `web-design-guidelines`.
- W4 ingestion: `architecture`, `api-patterns`, `testing-patterns`, `systematic-debugging`, security rules, document/PDF handling skills where safe.
- Testing: `tdd-workflow`, `testing-patterns`, `webapp-testing`, `lint-and-validate`, `verification-before-completion`.
- Security: `vulnerability-scanner`, `security-auditor`, `security-best-practices`, `security-threat-model` when explicitly requested or relevant.
- Debugging: `systematic-debugging`.
- Reviews: `code-review-checklist`, `requesting-code-review`, `receiving-code-review`.
- Planning: `plan-writing`, `writing-plans`, `executing-plans`.
- Git/work isolation: `using-git-worktrees` when work needs isolation.
- Parallelization: `parallel-agents` or `dispatching-parallel-agents` only under the Work Packet Register and only when tasks are independent.

## Exclusion Policy

Do not use or invoke excluded skills for MVP unless explicitly instructed by the human operator.

Exclude by default:

- mobile development/design skills;
- SEO/GEO skills;
- broad red-team or penetration-tester skills;
- behavioral-mode skills that conflict with LEXOS workflow discipline;
- intelligent-routing systems that bypass work packets;
- brainstorming skills when scope is already defined;
- autonomous orchestrator behavior not adapted to LEXOS.

## Conflict Rule

If imported skills conflict with LEXOS implementation docs, the LEXOS docs control.

If a skill suggests broad autonomous edits, global context ingestion, external communication, public storage, or skipping verification, do not follow it.

## Codex and Specialist Agent Rule

Codex and specialist agents are isolated workers only.

They must operate from:

- one work packet;
- one branch;
- defined file/folder scope;
- defined acceptance criteria;
- required final handoff.

No specialist agent may bypass `docs/implementation/05 Work Packet Register.md`.
